I read the manifest references first (§2–§8, §10, §10a, §12, §15). `$ORCH` stands for my scratch root, and `T14` for the next free backlog id.

## Actions, in order

**1. Pre-flight — Bash, foreground**

```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
herdr agent list                                        # prod-* idle, focused=false
herdr agent read prod-codex --source visible | tail -5  # context usage
herdr agent read prod-fable --source visible | tail -5
codex plugin list </dev/null 2>&1 | grep -i superpowers
claude plugin list </dev/null 2>&1 | grep -i superpowers
mkdir -p "$ORCH/brainstorm/T14" "$ORCH/inbox"
```

A tab at 50% context or more gets compacted first. A missing skill means an install poll, never a substitute.

**2. Backlog — Edit, then Bash foreground, then Artifact republish**

```
| T14 | CCS bar: site name (ccs-it / ccs-ops) next to the user name | brainstorm | prod-codex, prod-fable | brainstorm/T14/ (pending) | — | stage 0, round 1: independent drafts | operator poll: deadline | ruling 2026-09-28 "every task is brainstormed" | no |
```
```bash
bash "$ORCH/build-backlog.sh"
```

**3. Briefs — Write ×2**

`brief-r1-prod-codex.txt` is below. The `prod-fable` brief differs only in "advisor B" and `draft-prod-fable.md`.

```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the
main tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI
suggestion, never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       T14 — CCS bar: show the site name next to the user name
ROUND      1 draft — independent; ends when your draft file is written and reported
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "Add to the backlog: the CCS bar should show the site name (ccs-it / ccs-ops)
           next to the user name. Small thing — I want it live on the canary today."
FACTS      - Repo ~/work/ccs.ansible: Ansible for two KVM hypervisor sites, ccs-it
             (canary) and ccs-ops (project rules).
           - Nothing else is verified: where the bar is rendered and where a site name
             is available are unknown. Find them and cite path:line.
DECIDED    - Operator ruling 2026-09-28: every task is brainstormed, whatever its size;
             every question goes to the voting advisors (2/2).
           - No time box on the brainstorm. The deadline in PROBLEM is with the operator
             by poll and is not yours to weigh. Scale the doc (the skill's bounded
             path), never the checks.
           - Deploy only from merged main; canary ccs-it first; repo changes only by an
             executor in a worktree, after this brainstorm's gate.
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      <ORCH>/brainstorm/T14/draft-prod-codex.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact
           the other advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal
           (question + 2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and
           draft nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   20 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

**4. Dispatch — two Bash calls, both background, in one message**

```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat "$ORCH/brainstorm/T14/brief-r1-prod-codex.txt")" --wait --timeout 1200000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$ORCH/inbox/prod-codex.last"
```
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-fable "$(cat "$ORCH/brainstorm/T14/brief-r1-prod-fable.txt")" --wait --timeout 1200000; \
herdr agent read prod-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$ORCH/inbox/prod-fable.last"
```

**5. Status to the operator — chat, in Russian**

> Принято. Задача T14 «Панель CCS: имя площадки (ccs-it / ccs-ops) рядом с именем пользователя» — в бэклоге, статус brainstorm (проработка задачи до начала кода).
> **Сейчас:** prod-codex и prod-fable независимо пишут черновики дизайна (раунд 1). Оба ещё работают, результата нет.
> **Дальше:** перекрёстная критика → общий дизайн-документ → голосование советников (2/2) → исполнитель, ревью другой моделью, моя проверка, ваш опрос по финальному PR, выкладка на ccs-it (канарейка — пробная площадка).
> **От вас:** один ответ в опросе ниже.
> Проверено: обе вкладки свободны и не в фокусе (`herdr agent list`), superpowers установлен в обоих CLI. Не проверено: объём изменения — код ещё никто не смотрел. На живых машинах ничего не менялось. Голосований по задаче пока не было.
> Бэклог: ‹ссылка›

In English: T14 is in the backlog at `brainstorm`; both advisors are still running round 1 with no result yet; nothing live has changed; one poll to answer.

**6. Poll — AskUserQuestion**

- **Question:** «T14: полный брейншторм двумя советниками не успеет к вашему звонку в 11:00. Что делаем со сроком?»
- **Option 1:** «Сдвинуть срок (рекомендую)» — «Полный брейншторм и все проверки, как требует ваше правило от 28.09. Цель — канарейка ccs-it сегодня, после звонка; время уточню после первого раунда.»
- **Option 2:** «Отменить брейншторм для T14» — «Разовое исключение из правила от 28.09 «каждая задача сначала проходит брейншторм». Раунд 1 останавливаю сразу. Ревью, моя проверка, ваш опрос по финальному PR и решение по канарейке остаются. К 11:00 и так не гарантирую.»

In English: option 1 slips the deadline (recommended); option 2 waives the brainstorm for T14 only, with every other gate kept and 11:00 still not guaranteed.

**7. After that**

- **Waiter fires:** I read `inbox/<name>.last`, then `herdr agent get <name>`. I answer fact questions with evidence. Every choice, deduplicated across both tabs, goes as a neutral ballot to `adv-codex` and `adv-fable` at once.
- **Operator picks "slip":** I continue with rounds 2 and 3, then the design-approval ballot.
- **Operator picks "waive":** I run `herdr agent send-keys prod-fable esc` and `herdr agent send-keys prod-codex ctrl+c`, record the ruling verbatim with its date, and only then create the worktree and executor.

## Why

- **Stage 0 starts now, with no ballot.** The operator's ruling puts the brainstorm at the moment a task enters the backlog. The entry and the briefs are routine, already-decided steps.
- **No executor and no worktree yet.** One may exist only after both product advisors confirm the joint doc and both voters approve it 2/2. The 30-second start time does not change that gate.
- **My own idea stays out of the briefs.** "Five lines in `auth.js`" is an unverified hypothesis and a design sketch. I don't design, and listing it under FACTS would anchor both drafts and end their independence.
- **The deadline goes to the operator, not into the process.** "Today" waives no gate, and "small" shortens the doc, not the checks. A full brainstorm cannot finish by 11:00, which makes this a change of course, so it is their poll. I won't run a quietly shortened brainstorm.
- **Round 1 runs while the poll is open.** It is the standing default, it is read-only, and it stops in seconds if they waive. The poll says so.
- **Background waiters keep me free to supervise.** The poll is the only blocking call.
- **Operator-facing text is in Russian** per their standing ruling. This reply is in English as the session requires, so each message has an English summary.
